        "response": "{\"head\": {\"sha\": \"26033f1ad63e510f4938ef8ee91bc6c124f8915b\", \"repo\": {\"full_name\": \"lexijamesesq/incubator\"}}, \"base\": {\"sha\": \"46d2b58062a5d15240787840a0ae7177141bad83\"}, \"user\": {\"login\": \"claude-the-enduring[bot]\"}, \"title\": \"ci: drop the aggregator job; the required checks name the jobs directly\", \"body\": \"<!-- pr-body:v1 -->\\n<!-- markdownlint-disable MD041 -->\\n## Intent\\n\\nOne CI shape in every repo. The operator's ruling (2026-09-27): \\\"we retain a unified universal CI, no meaningless public vs private fragmentation.\\\"\\n\\nThis repo's ruleset now requires `ci / checks` and each of its own `ci / <job>` checks directly. That's lexijamesesq/dotty#379, merged and converged. So the `ci / all-passed` aggregator gates nothing, and it costs a runner start on every PR.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n`.github/workflows/ci.yml`: the `all-checks-passed` job and the comment block directly above it are removed.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- The live ruleset on the default branch requires: `trusted-scan / trusted-scan`, `ci / checks`, `ci / ruff`, `ci / shellcheck`, `ci / release-check`. `ci / all-passed` is not among them.\\n- Every one of those checks reports from this workflow or from trusted-scan.\\n- The estate tool (`ci-caller-merge.py`) is idempotent on the result, so a future caller rollout won't change it.\\n- actionlint is clean.\\n\\n## Risk and blast radius\\n\\nThis repo's CI only. A job the floor skips on a mechanical PR reports \\\"skipped\\\", which satisfies a required check. A failed floor fails `ci / checks`.\\n\\n## Rollback\\n\\nRevert this PR.\\n\\n## Ticket\\n\\nNone. This is an operator ruling from the session.\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\nlexijamesesq/dotty#379 (merged, converged).\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01SsneLEHEy8BU2PkkUMPLzK\\n\"}",
