              "actor_type": "RepositoryRole",
              "actor_id": 5,
              "bypass_mode": "pull_request"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Protect main — updates",
          "description": "The wall: only a designated merger may UPDATE main. Bypass = Ollie (4984137), the sole merger App, and the admin RepositoryRole (5) — both at pull_request mode (merge via PR, no standing direct-push bypass, per the estate's no-'always'-bypass invariant; a genuine emergency uses GitHub's admin override, not a persistent hole). Every other identity — the agent App, Renovate, any collaborator — cannot update main, so an approved PR merges only through Ollie. This is what makes reviewer-can't-merge and agent-can't-merge structural (the wall), not a matter of scope: Margot holds contents:write so its approval counts, and is kept from merging by being absent from THIS ruleset's bypass.",
          "rules": [
            "update"
          ],
          "bypass_actors": [
            {
              "actor_type": "Integration",
              "actor_id": 4984137,
              "bypass_mode": "pull_request"
            },
            {
              "actor_type": "RepositoryRole",
              "actor_id": 5,
              "bypass_mode": "pull_request"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
